    "created_at": "2019-07-23T20:10:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-07-23T20:10:05Z",
    "body": "> Sadly, we probably can’t just get rid of it, but we could maybe at least standardise Chrome’s behaviour\r\n\r\nI don't see how having an inconsistent behavior on `HTMLDocument` like Chrome does is more helpful to authors. Having consistency is good. Every inconsistency we introduce into the Web platform is yet another thing author has to deal with.",
