    "created_at": "2019-08-07T21:25:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-08-07T21:25:38Z",
    "body": "> We've got well over a week of data now, and for the last 7 days it's stable at about 3% of pageloads, on the Firefox nightly channel.\r\n\r\n3% is really high. For a comparison, the last time I checked, `attachShadow` (which is a function one must call to use shadow DOM) was used on only ~1.5% of page loads according to Chrome Platform Status. So named getters on document is used roughly twice as more frequently than the entirely of shadow DOM API.",
