    "created_at": "2026-11-07T14:16:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-07T14:16:44Z",
    "body": "> It's a little more complicated. Firefox implements `HTMLDocument` for `text/html` and `application/xhtml+xml`, whereas Safari and Chrome only do it for `text/html`, apparently...\n\nStill the case in Firefox Nightly, Chrome Canary and Safari TP. \n\nAlso, the spec's supported property names for `Document` don't depend on the document type, so `<embed name=\"foo\"/>` in an XHTML document should give `document.foo`; Firefox does that, and Chrome and Safari return undefined.\n\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
