    "created_at": "2026-11-09T12:38:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-10T06:47:02Z",
    "body": "I checked this with HTTP Archive and live page loads. I think Firefox should adopt the Chrome/Safari model: navigated XHTML documents become `XMLDocument`, with no named access. \n\nI found no breakage for Firefox, while the spec's current alias model, which no browser implements, breaks some widgets. Chrome lacks the named getter on HTML documents without a browsing context (https://crbug.com/594008), while Firefox and Safari TP have it. Chrome has shipped that way for about 10 years, and the bug (filed by bz) has 7 stars and no duplicates. Maybe the spec could drop it there instead?\n\nWith the Chrome/Safari model, `doc instanceof HTMLDocument` and `doc instanceof XMLDocument` distinguish text/html from XML documents (except `new Document()`, which is neither), as @mfreed7's XSLT polyfill assumed until mfreed7/xslt_polyfill#55 switched it to `contentType` for Firefox's XHTML.\n\nAI summary of the research ([zcorpan/htmldocument-compat-4792](https://github.com/zcorpan/htmldocument-compat-4792)):\n\n> Firefox Nightly 162, Chrome Canary 159 and Safari TP 255 were probed, and Safari TP matches Chrome Canary throughout. Changes were emulated with init scripts that log reads of changed values, or counted with a use counter in a Firefox build.\n>\n> | Change (HTTP Archive 2026-10-01) | Pages | Worse |\n> |---|---|---|\n> | XHTML as `XMLDocument` | 300 XML-typed root pages (150 XHTML) | 0 (≤2.9% of XHTML root pages) |\n> | No named access on XHTML | 683 XHTML URLs | 0 (≤0.6% of XHTML pages) |\n> | No named getter without a browsing context, random sample | 2,000 random desktop root pages | 0 (≤0.18% of desktop root pages) |\n> | No named getter without a browsing context, targeted sample | 2,000 XHR `responseXML` and 1,000 `parseHTMLUnsafe()` desktop root pages | 0 (≤0.003% and ≤0.0005% of desktop root pages) |\n> | Spec alias model, random sample | 500 mobile root pages | 0 (≤0.84% of mobile root pages) |\n> | Spec alias model, targeted sample | 155 pages with risky code patterns | 15 (insuit, on ~0.0034% of mobile root pages) |\n>\n> For the named getter, the targeted sample took pages from Blink's `XMLHttpRequestResponseXML` and `ParseHTMLUnsafe` use counters; pages using only `DOMParser` or `createHTMLDocument()` were sampled only at random.\n>\n> Under the alias model, the insuit accessibility widget (~500 mobile root pages, mostly Spanish government) loses its button ([image](https://github.com/zcorpan/htmldocument-compat-4792/blob/main/out-targeted-b2/review/100.png)), the Aniview video player isn't created, and react-tooltip 4.2.14–4.2.15 unmounts React apps. No browser has named properties in XML or SVG documents. The alias (2011, [W3C bug 14037](https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=14037)) was never implemented, and the members it shared now live on `Document`. [README](https://github.com/zcorpan/htmldocument-compat-4792/blob/main/README.md)\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
